From 441282af132f8e34e6f3f4ff23e721e75a8c7550 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:25:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/21] Support indirect draws and base vertex/instance with
 geometry shaders

vkCmdDrawIndirect and vkCmdDrawIndexedIndirect with a geometry-shader (mesh)
pipeline only logged 'not yet supported' and drew nothing (Xwayland's glamor
through zink issues indexed indirect draws with a geometry shader), and direct
draws ignored firstVertex, vertexOffset and firstInstance.

- A compute pass (cmdDrawIndirectGeometryConvertBuffers) converts each Vulkan
  indirect draw into mesh threadgroup counts (primitives x instances, by
  primitive type and list/strip) and the DrawInfo the object stage reads (index
  buffer address at firstIndex, base vertex, base instance). Each draw is then
  a drawMeshThreadgroupsWithIndirectBuffer with its DrawInfo bound as an object
  buffer.
- DrawInfo gains baseVertex and baseInstance (SPIRV-Cross patch adds them to
  the object stage); direct draws fill them from firstVertex / vertexOffset /
  firstInstance.
